Here's a clean, semantic structure:

```html
<article class="product-card">
  <img src="product.jpg" alt="Product Name" class="product-card__image">
  <div class="product-card__content">
    <h3 class="product-card__title">Product Name</h3>
    <p class="product-card__price">$29.99</p>
    <button class="product-card__button">Add to Cart</button>
  </div>
</article>
```

And the CSS:

```css
.product-card {
  background: white;
  border-radius: 8px;
  box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
  overflow: hidden;
}

.product-card__image {
  width: 100%;
  height: 200px;
  object-fit: cover;
}

.product-card__content {
  padding: 1rem;
}

.product-card__title {
  margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  font-size: 1.1rem;
}

.product-card__price {
  color: #2563eb;
  font-weight: bold;
  font-size: 1.25rem;
}

.product-card__button {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0.75rem;
  background: #2563eb;
  color: white;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 4px;
  cursor: pointer;
}
```

I'm using BEM naming convention - would you like me to explain why?

Can you review my code? I added a hover effect and made some changes:

```html
<article class="product-card">
  <img src="product.jpg" alt="Wireless Headphones" class="product-card__image">
  <div class="product-card__content">
    <h3 class="product-card__title">Wireless Headphones</h3>
    <p class="product-card__price">$79.99</p>
    <p class="product-card__description">Premium sound quality with 30-hour battery life</p>
    <button class="product-card__button">Add to Cart</button>
  </div>
</article>
```

```css
.product-card {
  background: white;
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
  overflow: hidden;
  transition: transform 0.2s, box-shadow 0.2s;
}

.product-card:hover {
  transform: translateY(-4px);
  box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.15);
}
```

Excellent work! Your additions are great:

✅ **Meaningful alt text** - "Wireless Headphones" instead of generic "Product Name"
✅ **Added description** - More context for users
✅ **Smooth hover effect** - The `translateY` lift is a nice touch
✅ **Transition on both properties** - Smooth shadow change too
✅ **Increased border-radius** - 12px looks more modern

**Suggestions:**

1. **Accessibility** - Add focus styles for keyboard users:
```css
.product-card:focus-within {
  outline: 2px solid #2563eb;
  outline-offset: 2px;
}
```

2. **Reduced motion** - Some users prefer less animation:
```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .product-card {
    transition: none;
  }
}
```

Would you like to add these accessibility improvements?

`prefers-reduced-motion` is a CSS media query that detects user preferences:

**How users enable it:**
- **macOS:** System Preferences → Accessibility → Display → Reduce motion
- **Windows:** Settings → Ease of Access → Display → Show animations
- **iOS:** Settings → Accessibility → Motion → Reduce Motion

**Why it matters:**
- Some people experience motion sickness from animations
- Users with vestibular disorders can feel dizzy
- It's part of WCAG accessibility guidelines

**Two values:**
```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { /* User wants less motion */ }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) { /* Default, animations OK */ }
```

**Best practice:** Design with motion, but provide a fallback for those who need it. Your hover effect is subtle enough that you could also just reduce the distance:

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .product-card:hover {
    transform: none; /* Remove the lift, keep the shadow change */
  }
}
```

The button hover isn't working - it's supposed to get darker but nothing happens. Here's my CSS:

```css
.product-card__button {
  background: #2563eb;
  color: white;
}

.product-card__button:hover {
  background: #1d4ed8;
}
```

Oh I found it! I had `pointer-events: none` on a parent container from earlier testing. Removed it and the hover works now. Thanks for walking me through the debugging process!

Here's my final code with all the accessibility improvements:

```css
.product-card__button {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0.75rem;
  background: #2563eb;
  color: white;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 4px;
  cursor: pointer;
  font-weight: 600;
  transition: background-color 0.2s;
}

.product-card__button:hover {
  background: #1d4ed8;
}

.product-card__button:focus {
  outline: 2px solid #1d4ed8;
  outline-offset: 2px;
}
```
